<speak>Yes, please keep the reminder simple. I receive so many messages that anything long gets mentally filed under 'read properly later', and later can become tomorrow. My family has a similar issue with the shared calendar. Someone writes a whole paragraph in an entry, and the important location is hidden at the bottom. We've started putting the basic information first. It's helped surprisingly much. I suppose a lot of household administration is just making the useful part easy to see when you're in a hurry.</speak>